{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VYyLYgFj9eu6SA8k7N21Xf","type":"tool_result","content":"278:## 16. A fitted slope is only \"cost per 1000 context\" if the mark is linear in context\n313:## 17. A launch that failed, and a `cudaStreamSynchronize` that called it success\n393:## 18. The device opt-in maximum is not the kernel's maximum, and the safety margin that failed a passing gate\n428:## 19. The variance is BETWEEN checkpoint loads, not within them — 0.6 % vs 5.7 %\n471:## 20. A gate that does not compile is a gate that passes by never running (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n519:## 21. dprof reads a saving 15–20 % low, so it attributes but does not ratchet (ladder 1.5)\n542:## 22. `tau` reproduced to four decimals; `tok/s` on the same protocol did not — and the promotion gate keys on the second one (ladder 2.2, 2026-08-20)\n606:## 23. A drift control that failed — and the agent that was contaminating its own arms (ladder 3.1, 2026-08-20)\n655:## 24. The base-AR window times the governor, not the engine — and it is 21 % (ladder 3.1, 2026-08-20)\n692:## 25. A unit gate that stops six times short of the regime it is quoted about (ladder 1.9, 2026-08-20)\n721:## 26. A field that was never computed compares equal, and equal reads as exonerated (ladder 1.9)\n749:## 27. `build/decode` and `dsv4-server` do not share a prefill, and a bit-exactness result on one says nothing about the other (ladder 1.9)\n=== kernel-opt ===\n14:## 1. The transformations that generalised\n67:## 2. Structural wins\n418:## 3. Precision and layout\n432:## 4. What every adopted change has in common\n=== negative ===\n52:## 3. The negatives that were really instrumentation failures\n71:## 4. Conditionally retired — re-open after the draft-head fine-tune\n88:## 4b. Killed inside the winning iteration — the radix top-k's two dead levers (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n119:## 4c. Adopted, bit-exact, and worth nothing — the `lim <= topk` early-out (ladder 1.3, 2026-08-20)