{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEUCLMV5Wx9RMwUmstXb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0196rhG3P6cuPu83hZ5PVyJL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -f evidence/decode_loop/build_1p7.done\ncat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p7.txt <<'EOF'\n1.7: sparse_attn stages the gathered KV row in shared memory -- 4.227 +/- 0.121 ms per forward,\n16 of 16 legs byte-identical, and it is the first item on this ladder to move term A\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED. One server load per arm, control arm FIRST so drift favours the control, four\nreps x three sweep contexts plus two control contexts. Control arm is\n`DSV4_SPARSE_HPB=1 DSV4_SPARSE_SMEM=0`, the pre-1.7 launch bit for bit, on the same binary.\n\n  ctx     ms/forward before -> after   paired    tok/s before -> after      tau\n  1,656   133.46 -> 130.33             -3.13     13.93 -> 14.27 (+2.44 %)   1.861 both\n  3,197   136.89 -> 132.78             -4.10     12.07 -> 12.44 (+3.07 %)   1.652 both\n  6,248   141.46 -> 137.05             -4.40     11.85 -> 12.23 (+3.21 %)   1.681 both\n  6,260   138.49 -> 134.20             -4.29     11.74 -> 12.13 (+3.32 %)   1.620 both\n  12,410  146.90 -> 142.24             -4.66     11.71 -> 12.09 (+3.25 %)   1.736 both\n\nEvery one of the 16 legs is faster, and all 16 emitted a BYTE-IDENTICAL text_sha256 with tau and\nmean verify width equal to four decimals -- at ctx up to 12,282, not at ctx 9. This satisfies the\nladder's PRIMARY bit-exactness invariant rather than its lossless-gate fallback.\n\nWHAT IT MEANS. Split at the knee the cost model predicts (topk = WINDOW(128) +\nmin(INDEX_TOPK(512), ctx/ratio) saturates at ctx 2048): -3.127 +/- 0.014 ms below it, -4.384 +/-\n0.065 above it, and above it delta = -3.996 +/- 0.080 flat -0.0552 +/- 0.0102 per 1000. So 94 % of\nthe win is the FLOOR -- which is exactly what this ladder entry predicted when it wrote \"the lever\nhere is the 11 ms FLOOR, not the slope, and it belongs to Term A as much as to Term B\".\n\n  a  129.11 -> 125.11 ms   (1.571x -> 1.522x the 82.18 ms byte floor; stop wants <= 1.25)\n  b  1.942  -> 1.887 /1000 (b x 6592: 12.80 -> 12.44 ms; stop wants <= 5.0; -74 % cumulative)\n\nSix items have moved b by 74 %. This is the first to move a at all, and a is 125.11 of a 142.24 ms\nforward at ctx 12,410 -- 88 % -- so it is where the remaining headroom is.\n\nThe 6 % that is not flat was PREDICTED FROM THE LAYER MAP BEFORE IT WAS FITTED, which is the only\nthing separating it from the artefact rule 7 exists to catch: 20 of 43 layers are ratio-128, and\ntheir topk = wmax + ctx/128 has no index_topk cap, so 20 x 7.81 rows per 1000 x 0.309 us saved per\nrow = 0.048 ms per 1000 predicted against 0.055 +/- 0.010 measured.\n\nTHE MECHANISM, and the part worth remembering: THE HYPOTHESIS IN THE LADDER ENTRY WAS WRONG. Both\nthe entry and B9's own comment blamed REUSE -- num_key_value_heads == 1, so topk_idxs is indexed by\n(b,m) and not by head, all 64 heads gather the identical rows, 63/64ths of 168 MB per compressed\nlayer is redundant. `hpb`, which is precisely the fix for that, already existed, and it is a\nMEASURED NULL: 1.00x at hpb=2 and hpb=4 at all six engine shapes. L1 was already catching it. The\nbinding constraint was instruction ISSUE: 32 scalar loads per warp per gathered row on a kernel\nwith 3-6 warps per SM and a 5-deep __shfl_down_sync chain with nothing to hide them behind. The fix\nis to stage the row in shared memory once per block with float4 loads and double buffering, hold it\nin registers across both consumers, and skip the expf when the running max did not move.\n\nVECTORISING THE GLOBAL LOAD WITHOUT LOSING BIT-EXACTNESS IS THE WHOLE TRICK. float4 normally\ndestroys it, because it changes which lane owns which element and therefore the shape of the\npartial-sum tree. Staging through smem decouples them: the load pattern becomes a pure\nmemory-PLACEMENT decision while the reduction still sees lane l holding {l, l+32, ..., l+480}, the\nsame 5-step shuffle tree, and the same online-softmax order over t. Every float operation, in every\norder, is the one the shipped kernel performed.\n\nAND THE OLD DEFAULT WAS A LIVE REGRESSION AT ITS OWN DESIGN POINT. B9 sized the hpb heuristic on a\n1022-token prefill and shipped HPB=8 there; measured today at that exact shape it is 0.80x, and at\nthe K=6 verify width 0.52x. Nothing had re-run the sweep after the shape moved. The new default\n(hpb=4, smem=2 below 1024 warps, smem=1 above) is 1.28x at that prefill and 1.21x at the short one,\nso this item also gives prefill back the 20 % the heuristic had been quietly costing it.\n\nTHE GATES. tests/gate_sparse_hpb.cu memcmps the ENTIRE output buffer of every (hpb, smem) launch\nagainst the pre-1.7 launch at six engine shapes -- 0 differing bytes -- and runs a one-ulp negative\ncontrol per shape that must fail. A cosine gate would pass exactly the defect this must catch,\nbecause sparse_attn sums the gathered rows IN ORDER under a non-associative online softmax. That\ncontrol earned itself immediately: on its first run it came back \"0 of 65536 floats differ\" at\ntopk=320, because the row it perturbed was not in that shape's gathered set -- a perturbation the\nkernel provably cannot see is not a control. Then gate_units, gate_indexer_decode,\ngate_compressed_decode, gate_prefill_len, gate_compressed_graph and gate_indexer_graph all at\nmaxabs = 0.00e+00; LOSSLESS GATE -> PASS x3; and both build/decode arms generated the identical ids\n11111 16 455 6102 294 16603 344 29168.\n\ndprof, both arms, ctx 3072/6144/12,288: cattn:sparse 18.66/19.38/20.57 -> 15.27/14.48/15.38, with\nthe parent ATTENTION falling 5.75 against the mark's 5.19 at ctx 12,288 and i:score, i:topk, o:rope\nand every moe:* mark unchanged -- no work relocated into an unmarked region. The before-arm also\nreproduces 0.4's original 19.22/19.90/21.17 four iterations and four kernel changes later.\n\nWiki, same iteration: kernel-optimisations.md 2.9 (adopted win), negative-results.md 4g (hpb alone,\nand the reuse hypothesis), measurement-and-traps.md 28 (a tuning default that expired), \ncontext-scaling.md (the 6 % Term-B tail), prefill-optimisation.md 7, README.md state table.\n\nDriver scripts/sparse_ab_run.sh, detached and named in detach_audit.sh's PATTERNS in this commit.\nEOF\ngit add -A && git status --short | wc -l","description":"Write commit message and stage"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":761,"cache_read_input_tokens":208977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":761},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8210199f-4413-4daf-85d7-08e4fdccb06e","uuid":"3d0cbbc3-6894-4a13-8752-a8120dc15e59","timestamp":"2026-08-20T18:25:52.975Z","request_id":"req_011CeEUCKMDCF8we9Ur1BmKy"}
